<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>Cookies Policy | Alpha Hill Medical Centre — Nandi County</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Cookies used by Alpha Hill Medical Centre’s website in Mosoriot, Nandi County: essential session cookies and optional first-party visit counts. Draft for legal review, August 2026."
    />
    <link rel="canonical" href="<%= site %>/cookies" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#001F5D" />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="Alpha Hill Medical Centre" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="Cookies Policy | Alpha Hill Medical Centre" />
    <meta
      property="og:description"
      content="How Alpha Hill Medical Centre uses cookies, how to accept or decline, and how to change your mind."
    />
    <meta property="og:url" content="<%= site %>/cookies" />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    <meta name="robots" content="index, follow" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/alphahillmedicallogo.png" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Manrope:wght@400;500;600;700;800&display=swap"
      rel="stylesheet"
    />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/styles.css" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <%- include('partials/public-header', { current: '' }) %>

    <main id="main">
      <section class="section">
        <div class="container policy">
          <p class="breadcrumb">
            <a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span>Cookies Policy
          </p>
          <p class="eyebrow">Your choices</p>
          <h1>Cookies Policy</h1>
          <p class="lead">
            This draft is provided for the owner’s legal review. Last updated
            August 2026.
          </p>

          <h2>Who we are</h2>
          <p>
            This policy explains how the website of Alpha Hill Medical Centre,
            Mosoriot, Nandi County, uses cookies. Contact us at
            <a href="mailto:alphahillmedical@gmail.com">alphahillmedical@gmail.com</a>
            or
            <a href="tel:+254722865459">+254 722 865 459</a>. Our
            <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> describes how we handle
            personal information more generally.
          </p>

          <h2>What cookies are</h2>
          <p>
            Cookies are small text files stored on your device by a website.
            They can remember a choice you have made or keep you signed in.
            This site sets cookies itself (first-party cookies). We do not
            allow Google Analytics, Facebook Pixel, Hotjar, Microsoft Clarity
            or similar third-party trackers.
          </p>

          <h2>Cookies we use</h2>
          <h3>Essential</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Staff sign-in</strong> (<code>ahmc.sid</code>) — used only
              on the private dashboard so authorised staff stay signed in after
              entering a one-time email code. It lasts two days or until
              sign-out, and is not set for ordinary visitors.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Cookie choice</strong> (<code>ahmc_consent</code>) —
              remembers whether you accepted or declined the optional visitor
              identifier so we do not ask on every page. This cookie is set when
              you use the banner.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <h3>Optional analytics (only after you Accept)</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Visitor identifier</strong> (<code>ahmc_vid</code>) — a
              random number, stored with the pages you open, that lets us tell
              how many separate people visit rather than only how many pages
              are opened. We do not store your IP address and we do not store
              your User-Agent.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <h2>Counting page visits without cookies</h2>
          <p>
            We keep a simple tally of how many times each public page is
            opened. Each entry is only the page address and the date and time.
            It contains nothing that identifies you — no cookie, no account, no
            IP address, no device or browser details — so it cannot be traced
            back to you or joined up with anything else, and it does not
            require your consent.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you choose <strong>Decline</strong>, we do not set the visitor
            identifier, so we cannot tell your pages apart from anyone else's.
            The anonymous page tally continues, and the website, forms and
            WhatsApp link all work as normal.
          </p>

          <h2>How long they last</h2>
          <p>
            If you accept, your choice and the visitor identifier are stored for
            up to 12 months. If you decline, we remember that for three months
            and then ask once more. The staff session cookie lasts two days from
            sign-in, or until you sign out.
          </p>

          <h2>How to change your mind</h2>
          <p>
            Use Accept or Decline on the banner. To withdraw analytics consent
            later, clear cookies for alphahillmedical.co.ke in your browser, or
            email
            <a href="mailto:alphahillmedical@gmail.com">alphahillmedical@gmail.com</a>
            and we will help you. You can also block cookies in your browser
            settings; essential staff login will then not work until cookies
            are allowed for that page.
          </p>

          <h2>This is not a medical-records site</h2>
          <p>
            Cookies on this website are for running the site and, if you agree,
            recognising a repeat visitor. They are not used to store clinical
            notes. Please
            do not send sensitive health details through public forms.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <%- include('partials/public-footer') %>
    <script src="/assets/js/main.js"></script>
  </body>
</html>
